<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12490" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĕcĭmātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		decimo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the taking of a tenth</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A tithing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Tobiae, 1, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A selecting by lot of every tenth man for
				punishment, decimation</i>, <i><span class="en">Capitol.
				Macr. 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A tenth</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adhuc in ea decimatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 6, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
